+// Deterministic mode (netplay and its sync test): events from outside the
+// game's threads (retraces, RSP and display list completions, controller
+// reads) reach the game only when all its threads wait, in a fixed order,
+// and the game's time (retraces, the CPU counter, audio played) moves on
+// there, one retrace at a time, instead of with the host's clock. Given the
+// same input, the game then does the same thing however fast the PC is.
+// Set before the game starts.
+void set_deterministic(bool on);
+bool is_deterministic();
+uint64_t deterministic_vi_count();
+void deterministic_vi_tick();
+// The screen shown again as it is (the game waiting, for the other player in
+// netplay, while what's drawn over it changes).
+void deterministic_present();
+void wait_for_deterministic_tasks();
+void deterministic_audio_tick();
+
 // Thread scheduling.
 void check_running_queue(RDRAM_ARG1);
 void run_next_thread_and_wait(RDRAM_ARG1);
